{"key":"hf4-apphycem-mcq-003-v2","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"B","final_answer":"0 N·m²/C","working":"According to Gauss's Law, the net electric flux through any closed surface is proportional to the net charge enclosed by the surface: Φ = Q_enc / ε_0. The enclosed charges are +4.0 nC and -4.0 nC, giving a net enclosed charge Q_enc = +4.0 nC + (-4.0 nC) = 0 C. Charges outside the surface (such as the +6.0 nC charge) do not contribute to the net electric flux through the closed surface. Thus, Φ = 0 N·m²/C.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":420,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":420,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":405,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":163,"reasoningTokens":242},"totalTokens":825,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":242,"promptTokenCount":420,"candidatesTokenCount":163,"totalTokenCount":825,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":420}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":163}]},"reasoningTokens":242,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":3700,"keyed_label":"B"}
