{"key":"hf4-apphycem-mcq-003-v1","kind":"mcq","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"B","final_answer":"0 N·m²/C","working":"By Gauss’s law, the net electric flux through any closed surface is Φ_net = Q_enc/ε₀. The cube contains no charge, so Q_enc = 0 and thus Φ_net = 0. Equivalently, the uniform field enters one perpendicular face and exits the opposite face with equal magnitude, so the inward and outward fluxes cancel; the other four faces have zero flux because the field is parallel to them.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":457,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":201,"cacheReadTokens":256},"outputTokens":343,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":128,"reasoningTokens":215},"totalTokens":800,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":457,"completion_tokens":343,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":256,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":201,"total_tokens":800,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":256},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":215}},"reasoningTokens":215,"cachedInputTokens":256},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":4448,"keyed_label":"B"}
